 R←Test_Misc_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;S
⍝ Exercise `SplitProjectUrl`: a project URL need not have the expected shape.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 S←##.GitHub.SplitProjectUrl

 ⍝ The ordinary case, and the variations that are still fine:
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub/'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'http://github.com/aplteam/GitHub'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'github.com/aplteam/GitHub'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://www.github.com/aplteam/GitHub'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://GitHub.COM/aplteam/GitHub'

 ⍝ A trailing ".git" does not belong to the repository's name:
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub.git'

 ⍝ Anything below the repository is none of our business:
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub/blob/main/README.md'
 →T.PassesIf('aplteam' 'GitHub' '')≡S'https://github.com/aplteam/GitHub/issues/1'

 ⍝ And what must be refused rather than taken apart regardless:
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢3⊃S'https://gitlab.com/someone/Thing'
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢3⊃S'https://github.com/aplteam'      ⍝ No repository at all
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢3⊃S''
 →T.PassesIf 0<≢3⊃S'https://'
 ⍝ …and in every one of those, owner and repo must be empty rather than wrong:
 →T.PassesIf∧/0=≢¨2↑S'https://gitlab.com/someone/Thing'
 →T.PassesIf∧/0=≢¨2↑S'https://github.com/aplteam'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
